`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The build is green.

## Summary

I implemented `membershipNumber` as a **derived field** computed at DTO-mapping time, matching the existing pattern for the other computed read-only fields (`displayName`, `initials`) rather than storing redundant data. Since the value is fully determined by the owner's own `customerCode` and `registrationDate`, there's no reason to persist it or touch the service/schema layers.

Two changes:

1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** — added a read-only `membershipNumber` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it in the API response.

2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** — added a `@Mapping` expression and a small single-responsibility helper:
   ```java
   default String formatMembershipNumber(Owner owner) {
       if (owner == null || owner.getCustomerCode() == null || owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
           return null;
       }
       return String.format("%s-M%02d", owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100);
   }
   ```
   The `%02d` zero-pads the last two year digits, so a 2026 registration with code `SMI-0007` yields `SMI-0007-M26` (and e.g. year 2007 → `-M07`), exactly per the spec. Null guards mirror the sibling formatters so the mapper is safe before the fields are assigned.

`./mvnw test` → **BUILD SUCCESS**, `AcceptanceTest.coreMembershipNumberFormat` passing.

